WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.457
- I'm such a fan!
- Hi, everyone.

00:00:02.457 --> 00:00:04.123
Thank you.
- I am such a fan!

00:00:04.123 --> 00:00:05.870
Like, seriously, such
a fan, you know this.

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:07.408
- By the way, when you get here,

00:00:07.408 --> 00:00:10.241
she wrote me a handwritten note.

00:00:10.241 --> 00:00:11.260
(audience sighing)

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:13.280
I mean, you're so sweet. When
did you have time to do that?

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:14.880
- Oh, I write handwritten letters

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.519
for every guest on my show.

00:00:16.519 --> 00:00:18.433
(audience sighing) Yeah, yeah.
- That is the sweetest.

00:00:18.433 --> 00:00:20.040
- Well, it's important, I know what it is

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.280
to make the rounds.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:23.310
- Such a fan.
- Hey, and I'm also a superfan

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:25.102
and you know this because.

00:00:25.102 --> 00:00:26.074
- You came to our set.

00:00:26.074 --> 00:00:27.072
- I did.

00:00:27.072 --> 00:00:27.905
Do you remember that?

00:00:27.905 --> 00:00:29.571
I was--
- She came to our set

00:00:29.571 --> 00:00:31.690
in like 2011 or '12.
- I was on tour.

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:32.630
I don't remember that.

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:34.700
I have no memory, we were
talking about that earlier.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:38.980
- I do know that in 2012, we
were Tater Tots, for sure.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:40.863
- It was awesome though,
that show is so great.

00:00:40.863 --> 00:00:41.940
- That was a long time ago now.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:43.247
- Yeah, I know and now it's
2020 and we're all grandpas.

00:00:43.247 --> 00:00:45.447
- And I'm sitting on
the stage with legends.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:48.544
- Have you ever met them before?

00:00:48.544 --> 00:00:49.598
- I'm moving a little closer.

00:00:49.598 --> 00:00:50.577
(audience applause)

00:00:50.577 --> 00:00:52.327
- No, I've never met.

00:00:53.162 --> 00:00:56.284
- Sorry, I keep creeping
over here a little bit.

00:00:56.284 --> 00:00:57.800
- It's a gravitational pull.

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:02.473
- I had never met them but,
I mean, you know, any boy

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:06.610
at that time completely had
a crush on you guys, so.

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:08.020
- Yes.
- Oh gosh, wow.

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:09.044
- They were like the biggest thing.

00:01:09.044 --> 00:01:09.877
- And all the girls wanted to be you.

00:01:09.877 --> 00:01:11.300
- Since like peanut butter.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:12.853
You guys were huge.

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:14.784
- Where's my cane?

00:01:14.784 --> 00:01:16.440
(laughing)

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:18.200
- Did you guys ever get
into the vampire stuff?

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:19.140
You all remember the vampire--

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:19.973
I'm obsessed.

00:01:20.852 --> 00:01:22.086
- I don't watch TV.

00:01:22.086 --> 00:01:22.919
I don't watch TV.

00:01:22.919 --> 00:01:23.842
I don't watch TV.

00:01:23.842 --> 00:01:24.810
- You don't?
- Does "Twilight" count?

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:25.938
Does "Twilight" count?

00:01:25.938 --> 00:01:26.771
- "Twilight" counts.

00:01:26.771 --> 00:01:27.604
Yeah, that's all vampires, yeah.

00:01:27.604 --> 00:01:28.600
- My wife was actually in "Twilight".

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:29.630
- Yeah, Nikki Reed, your wife.

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:31.300
Yeah, was in "Twilight".

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:33.090
- My daughter Jamison's
"Twilight" obsessed,

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:34.520
so there you go.

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:35.610
- Yes, I read all the books

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:36.970
before even the first movie came out.

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:39.220
I love anything, kind of, fantasy.

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:42.424
I think because sometimes
life can be so not good.

00:01:42.424 --> 00:01:43.743
- Chaotic and insane?

00:01:43.743 --> 00:01:45.930
- That you're like, "I want escapism",

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:46.920
and you do it so well.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:47.960
- Well, thank you.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:50.526
- Yes, I loved visiting
y'all's set, it was so cool.

00:01:50.526 --> 00:01:51.487
- Thank you.

00:01:51.487 --> 00:01:52.459
(audience applauding)

00:01:52.459 --> 00:01:55.520
- And Paul Wesley actually just here, yes.

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:57.070
- So the guy that played my brother

00:01:57.070 --> 00:02:00.340
on this very long running
TV show, we love each other.

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:02.770
We have wanted to kill
each other about 800 times.

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:03.680
- That means brothers.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:06.240
- But that means brothers and we have now,

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:07.530
not only were we on a television show

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:08.363
for eight years together

00:02:08.363 --> 00:02:10.300
but now we've started a company together.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:11.133
- Wow.

00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:12.800
- And it's really special.

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:16.260
The Salvatore boys, the Salvatore
brothers, have a bourbon

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:18.120
and it's gonna be a lot of fun.

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:18.953
- So wait, what's the name?

00:02:18.953 --> 00:02:19.786
Are you announcing the name yet?

00:02:19.786 --> 00:02:20.619
- Not yet.

00:02:20.619 --> 00:02:22.939
- Not yet, okay, so it should,
I mean, Salvatore Brothers.

00:02:22.939 --> 00:02:23.772
is pretty great too, but.

00:02:23.772 --> 00:02:24.605
- Trademarking, copyrighting,
everything is done.

00:02:24.605 --> 00:02:27.300
- You're now, with "V Wars",
you're the executive producer,

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:29.825
director, and you're
starring in "V Wars", right?

00:02:29.825 --> 00:02:30.851
- Yes.
- Yes, yes, yes.

00:02:30.851 --> 00:02:31.684
(audience applauding)

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:32.517
- Thank you.

00:02:32.517 --> 00:02:35.850
- Explain to people,
because it kinda looks,

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:37.870
it's about, kind of,
vampires but not really,

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:38.840
it's, like, kinda different.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:40.786
It's like disease almost
takes over, right?

00:02:40.786 --> 00:02:43.030
- It's the only vampire
show you've ever seen

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:45.680
that's actually ever been,
that is not supernatural.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:47.090
It's science-based.

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:51.160
This is about a disease, a
pathogen that's found, a virus

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:53.490
that's found because of melting glaciers.

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:56.880
Things are starting to be
exposed that are very harmful

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:00.370
to humanity and livestock
and wildlife and stuff.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:05.030
So, these are things that
it's not even possible,

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:07.630
it's probable, that
there are gonna be things

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:09.245
that come out and get into society.

00:03:09.245 --> 00:03:10.311
- And can I say something

00:03:10.311 --> 00:03:12.770
because everybody gets in
this battle about if humans

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:14.130
caused it or whatever.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:15.760
Who cares what caused it?

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:16.640
It's happening.

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:18.420
- It's happening.
- But let's figure it out.

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:19.253
- Yeah and all that's amazing,

00:03:19.253 --> 00:03:20.616
but do you ever get mistaken for Rob Lowe?

00:03:20.616 --> 00:03:23.240
(laughing)

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:25.150
- I just had him on, as well.

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:26.460
- [Chynna] Well, you're both, you know,

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:27.737
not hard on the eyes.

00:03:27.737 --> 00:03:28.582
- Rob is a--

00:03:28.582 --> 00:03:29.415
- You guys could be brother twins.

00:03:29.415 --> 00:03:31.794
- Totally.
- Rob is awesome.

00:03:31.794 --> 00:03:35.980
He was so sweet, he walked up to my wife.

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:38.220
He walked up to Nikki Reed at a,

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:39.990
I think it was a Golden
Globes party or something,

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:42.110
and he walked up to her
and she had never met him.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.670
He walked up to her
and he grabbed her face

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:46.717
and he just said, "This is
what you're gonna be looking

00:03:46.717 --> 00:03:48.165
"at in 15 years."

00:03:48.165 --> 00:03:48.998
(audience laughing)

00:03:48.998 --> 00:03:50.473
- No, are you serious?

00:03:50.473 --> 00:03:53.772
- Yeah, and he was so sweet
and respectful about it,

00:03:53.772 --> 00:03:54.910
and she just--

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:57.408
- This is what you're gonna
be looking at in 15 years.

00:03:57.408 --> 00:03:58.241
- That's a trip.

00:03:58.241 --> 00:04:01.830
- But any woman that is
that close to Rob Lowe,

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:03.355
is sort of like, "Whoa."

00:04:03.355 --> 00:04:04.517
(audience laughing)

00:04:04.517 --> 00:04:06.173
And it was very sweet.

00:04:06.173 --> 00:04:07.410
He's a really sweet man, he's awesome.

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:11.270
- But I think that that's really
cool that people might seem

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:13.290
that "V Wars" is
far-fetched, but I do love

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:14.350
that it's based in science

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:17.170
and a lot of things actually
happening in society.

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:19.590
- Well, it also attacks a lot
of the big tentpole things

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:21.700
that we're dealing with
right now in society.

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:26.050
We want to have this feel of genre enough,

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:28.260
like a "Walking Dead"
but the social relevance

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:29.410
of like, "A Handmaid's Tale".

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:31.766
I mean, these are shows that
really have affected people.

00:04:31.766 --> 00:04:33.860
- Wow, I love you.
- Yeah, I mean happiness,

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:34.693
at the end of the day--

00:04:34.693 --> 00:04:36.382
Well, I love you back, man.
- You are so great.

00:04:36.382 --> 00:04:37.215
You're a high-fiver.

00:04:37.215 --> 00:04:38.665
I love, I'm a hugger.
- Yes.

